  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0045-p00045",
      "source_en": "I need not the vast sky of sea and open heavens, nor do I wish to send up a great paper kite to roam the sky and tease the winds from every side; I need only one minute. I need only a little light. I need only one narrow slit, like a child crawling on hands and knees, at the window of a dark room, watching the unending slit at the edge of the western sky, one little point of light, one minute.",
